// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// GO-LIVE READY — DO NOT APPLY UNTIL LLEWELLYN SAYS GO. Review + apply manually.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Veld & Carrying Capacity — Phase 5 go-live ruleset (MERGE FRAGMENT).
//
// THIS FILE IS NOT A COMPLETE RULESET. It must NOT replace `firestore.rules`.
// It is the set of blocks to paste INTO the live `firestore.rules`, inside
// `match /databases/{database}/documents { ... }`, immediately ABOVE the
// existing default-deny catch-all:
//
//     match /{document=**} {
//       allow read, write: if false;
//     }
//
// That catch-all must remain the LAST block. It is the default-deny that keeps
// every un-listed path closed, and the veld feature relies on it for its dark
// (flag-OFF) posture.
//
// ── Why this file exists (DRAFT → GO_LIVE_READY) ─────────────────────────
// `firestore.rules.veld_carry.DRAFT` was written in Phase 0D, BEFORE the real
// repository existed, and it nests the veld data under the TOP-LEVEL
// `farms/{farmId}` collection. The Phase 2+ code does NOT use that layout. The
// shipped repository (`lib/features/veld_carry/veld_carry_repository.dart`)
// nests everything under the signed-in outfitter's OWN user document:
//
//   users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId}
//   users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId}/stock/{entryId}
//   users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId}/plantedAreas/{areaId}
//   users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId}/predators/{predatorId}
//   users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/permits/{permitId}
//
// These paths are the authoritative contract (see `VeldCarryRepository.campPath`
// / `stockPath` / `plantedAreaPath` / `predatorPath` / `permitPath`, and the
// collection-name constants `usersCollection` / `farmsCollection` /
// `campsCollection` = 'veldCamps' / `stockCollection` / `plantedAreasCollection`
// / `predatorsCollection` / `permitsCollection`). Applying the old DRAFT would
// leave every real veld read/write denied by the default-deny catch-all.
//
// ── Ownership model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The PATH carries the owner: the second segment is the outfitter's uid, and
// Firestore guarantees a caller cannot write a path they were not granted. So
// ownership is `request.auth.uid == outfitterUid` — a single, non-spoofable
// check that needs no `get()` and no owner field on the child documents.
// (The DRAFT instead read `farms/{farmId}.outfitterId`; that indirection is
// gone because the top-level farm document is not on the veld data path.)
//
// ── Deliberate omissions (unchanged from the DRAFT's security posture) ───
//   • NO public read anywhere — no read grant in this file is unconditional.
//   • NO hunter write anywhere — every create/update/delete is owner-only.
//   • NO hunter read on `predators` — predator records stay outfitter-only.
//   • NO admin bypass on camps / stock / plantedAreas / predators / permits.
//     The brief is "owner read/write only"; add `|| isAdmin()` only if
//     Llewellyn approves it explicitly at go-live.
//   • NO farm-manager access. `farm_managers` assigns a manager to a farm;
//     wiring managers in is a separate go-live decision.
//
// ── Validation performed on this file ────────────────────────────────────
//   • braces balanced, parens balanced (see the Phase 5 hand-back).
//   • no unconditional read grant anywhere (no bare-true read, alone or paired
//     with write).
//   • default-deny in the live ruleset verified intact and untouched.
//   • every path below matches the repository's path builders exactly.
//
// ── Known limitation (documented in docs/veld_carry_go_live_checklist.md) ─
// FIXED in Phase 6 (commit: "fix(veld): Phase 6 — hunter permits query fix +
// permit Storage upload + booking check"). The hunter permit read is gated on
// `resource.data.visibility`, which Firestore can only honour for a QUERY that
// constrains the same field. `VeldCarryRepository.getPermitsForHunter` now
// issues `.where('visibility', isEqualTo: 'hunter_visible')` and keeps the
// client-side `hunterVisiblePermits` filter as a second line of defence
// (veld_carry_repository.dart, method `getPermitsForHunter`). An unconstrained
// read would have been rejected with `permission-denied`.
//
// ── Booking check (go-live relationship gate) ───────────────────────────
// PHASE 7D UPDATE — the relationship gate is NOW EXPRESSIBLE IN RULES.
//
// A rule still may not read another collection (`bookings`), so the booking
// relationship is DENORMALISED instead: `allowedHunterUids` (List<String>) is
// written onto every camp document of the farm by
// `VeldCarryRepository.syncAllowedHuntersForFarm`, which collects the hunters
// holding a CONFIRMED / COMPLETED booking on that farm.
//
// The camps / stock / plantedAreas rules below therefore gate on
//     request.auth.uid in resource.data.allowedHunterUids
// (stock + plantedAreas resolve the field from their parent camp with a
// `get()`; the camp path is fully specified by the query, so `get()` is valid
// for a LIST query as well as a single-document read).
//
// ⚠️ APPLY-TIME PREREQUISITE — Firestore rules are NOT filters. A rule that
// inspects `resource.data.allowedHunterUids` can only serve a QUERY that
// constrains the same field (this is the same trap as the Phase 6 permit
// blocker, §7.2). Before this file is applied, the hunter camp read in
// `VeldCarryRepository.getCampsForHunter` must add
//
//     .where('allowedHunterUids', arrayContains: hunterUid)
//
// (stock / plantedAreas need no change: their rule resolves the field through a
// `get()` on the fully-specified parent camp path, which is constant across the
// query). Without that constraint Firestore rejects the hunter's camp LIST read
// with `permission-denied`. The client query is deliberately NOT changed in
// Phase 7D because the rules are NOT applied yet — changing it now would deny
// hunters on farms whose sync has not run.
//
// IMPORTANT — this closes the Phase 5/6 residual exposure ONLY ONCE THE SYNC
// HAS RUN. The allow-list is data, not code:
//   • a camp that has never been synced has NO `allowedHunterUids` field, and
//     every non-owner read of it is DENIED (the `in` on a missing field errors,
//     which fails closed);
//   • the outfitter re-runs the sync from the camp list ("Sync hunter access",
//     Phase 7D) — there is NO automatic booking-confirmation hook yet, by
//     design (see docs/veld_carry_go_live_checklist.md §7.3);
//   • removals are deliberately NOT automatic: cancelling a booking does not
//     revoke access. Keeping access is the safer failure mode, and revoking is
//     an explicit operator action.
//
// The code-side `hunterHasBookingForFarm` gate stays in place as the primary
// enforcement (defence in depth): it fails closed on every `...ForHunter` read
// when a `hunterUid` is supplied.
//
// FALLBACK: if the allow-list sync is NOT adopted, restore the Phase 5 rule —
// `allow read: if isSignedIn();` — which is kept commented in each block. That
// restores the documented Phase 6 posture (any signed-in hunter who knows the
// `outfitterUid` + `farmId` can read hunter-safe veld data).

//
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// [MERGE] helper — add next to the existing isSignedIn() / isOwnerOf() helpers
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    // True when the caller owns the veld document they are addressing.
    // The owner is the uid in the path (`users/{outfitterUid}/...`), so no
    // document read is needed and a missing parent document cannot widen
    // access.
    function isVeldOwner(outfitterUid) {
      return isSignedIn() && request.auth.uid == outfitterUid;
    }

    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // [MERGE] helper — Phase 7D allow-list gate for a camp CHILD document
    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    //
    // Stock and plantedAreas carry no allow-list of their own; it lives on the
    // parent camp. The camp path is fully specified by the caller's query, so
    // this single-document `get()` is valid for both a single read and a LIST
    // query. A missing camp document, or a camp with no `allowedHunterUids`,
    // errors and therefore DENIES (fail closed).
    function isAllowedCamper(outfitterUid, farmId, campId) {
      return isSignedIn()
        && request.auth.uid in get(
          /databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(outfitterUid)
            /farms/$(farmId)/veldCamps/$(campId)
        ).data.allowedHunterUids;
    }

    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // [MERGE] veldCamps — owner full read/write; hunter read via allow-list
    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    //
    // NOTE the collection is `veldCamps`, NOT `camps` (the DRAFT's name).
    match /users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId} {
      // Phase 7D: the booking relationship is now enforced HERE, from the
      // denormalised allow-list that `syncAllowedHuntersForFarm` writes.
      // See the "Booking check" note in this file's header.
      allow read: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        || (isSignedIn()
            && resource.data.keys().hasAny(['allowedHunterUids'])
            && resource.data.allowedHunterUids is list
            && request.auth.uid in resource.data.allowedHunterUids);

      // FALLBACK (Phase 5 posture — booking gate in CODE only):
      // allow read: if isSignedIn();

      // A camp document may never claim a farmId other than its own path
      // segment. `request.resource` is null on delete, so the payload check is
      // scoped to create/update and delete gets its own owner-only grant.
      allow create, update: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        && request.resource.data.farmId == farmId;
      allow delete: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid);
    }

    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // [MERGE] stock ledger — owner full read/write; hunter read (interim)
    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    match /users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId}/stock/{entryId} {
      // Phase 7D: gated by the camp's denormalised allow-list (the stock row
      // carries none of its own). See the "Booking check" header note.
      allow read: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        || isAllowedCamper(outfitterUid, farmId, campId);

      // FALLBACK (Phase 5 posture — booking gate in CODE only):
      // allow read: if isSignedIn();

      // A stock row may never claim a campId other than its own path segment.
      allow create, update: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        && request.resource.data.campId == campId;
      allow delete: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid);
    }

    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // [MERGE] plantedAreas — owner full read/write; hunter read (interim)
    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    //
    // Hunter read is granted because the hunter-facing capacity total includes
    // year-round planted feed (feed type + hectares are not sensitive).
    match /users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId}/plantedAreas/{areaId} {
      // Phase 7D: gated by the camp's denormalised allow-list. See the
      // "Booking check" header note.
      allow read: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        || isAllowedCamper(outfitterUid, farmId, campId);

      // FALLBACK (Phase 5 posture — booking gate in CODE only):
      // allow read: if isSignedIn();

      // A planted area may never claim a campId other than its own path
      // segment.
      allow create, update: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        && request.resource.data.campId == campId;
      allow delete: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid);
    }

    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // [MERGE] predators — OWNER ONLY. No hunter read, by design.
    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    //
    // Predator pressure is outfitter-internal management data (species, counts,
    // prey offtake). The hunter view never queries this collection
    // (`VeldCarryRepository` exposes no `...ForHunter` predator read), so no
    // hunter clause exists — and none may be added without an explicit
    // go-live decision.
    match /users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/veldCamps/{campId}/predators/{predatorId} {
      allow read: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid);

      // A predator record may never claim a campId other than its own path
      // segment.
      allow create, update: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        && request.resource.data.campId == campId;
      allow delete: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid);
    }

    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // [MERGE] permits — owner full read/write; hunter read on visible permits
    // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    //
    // Permits are farm-wide (not camp-specific), so they hang directly off the
    // farm document.
    match /users/{outfitterUid}/farms/{farmId}/permits/{permitId} {
      // The owning outfitter reads every permit on their farm.
      //
      // A signed-in non-owner reads a permit ONLY when the outfitter marked it
      // `hunter_visible`. This is the interim gate.
      //
      // Phase 7D — allow-list variant, NOT enabled yet (see below):
      //   allow read: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
      //     || (isSignedIn()
      //         && resource.data.visibility == 'hunter_visible'
      //         && resource.data.keys().hasAny(['allowedHunterUids'])
      //         && request.auth.uid in resource.data.allowedHunterUids);
      // Permits are FARM-level (not camp-level) and the camp sync does not
      // write onto them, so enabling this clause today would deny every hunter
      // permit read. Enable it only once the permit write stamps the farm's
      // allow-list (a Phase 8 item). Until then this block keeps the Phase 6
      // visibility gate, with the code-side booking check as the real gate.
      //
      // FIXED in Phase 6 (code, not rules): a `resource.data` condition can
      // only be honoured for a QUERY that constrains the same field, and
      // `VeldCarryRepository.getPermitsForHunter` now issues
      // `.where('visibility', isEqualTo: 'hunter_visible')` (plus a
      // defence-in-depth Dart filter). This rule can now serve that read.
      allow read: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        || (isSignedIn() && resource.data.visibility == 'hunter_visible');

      // Writes stay owner-only. No hunter write, no manager write.
      // A permit may never claim a farmId other than its own path segment.
      allow create, update: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid)
        && request.resource.data.farmId == farmId;
      allow delete: if isVeldOwner(outfitterUid);
    }

